      "description": "Guilt is the real moral condition of having actually done wrong — not merely feeling bad but being genuinely culpable. The Hebrew vocabulary of guilt is closely tied to the guilt offering, the sacrifice that addresses the actual debt. The New Testament Greek (syneidēsis, conscience) addresses the inner knowing of one's own guilt. Guilt is real before it is felt: the question of whether one feels guilty is separate from the question of whether one is guilty. Scripture addresses both the fact and the experience, and offers genuine resolution for both.",
